From 405db45275a879d16a84ca1898f349c19953133c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:44:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] classes: natives as classes - the embedder's door (citadel
 r3, patch 34)

- native method entries fly: run_native (one shared flight, arity-bounds
  checked against ok_native_fn's 8-bit argc - the old call_native would
  truncate then overrun its stash on a 256+ argument ANY-arity call) and
  call_native_method (receiver rides argv[0], the INVOKE/bound-method/
  operator-dispatch window shape). all seven 'native methods arrive with
  the native-class patch' traps are now the real lanes: INVOKE,
  SUPER_INVOKE, bound methods, the instance and static call operators,
  the operator dispatch, and a C-defined init
- the builtin receivers dispatch on their class singletons: a.len() maps
  through classof, mic-cached like any site (sealed tables, C15). the
  error message for a missing method on a native names the class now
- the surfaces (no new stdlib, per the ruling): array len/push/pop/
  remove, map len/remove/get - the SAME C entries the free-function
  spellings use, mounted twice. str/function/num/bool/nil stay empty in
  v0.5.0: nothing existed to mirror
- the embedder's C API: ok_class_new (unfrozen, parent or null=Object),
  ok_class_define_native_method (arity counts the receiver, pub flag,
  one-name-one-owner + pub-survives + dispatch-arity contract enforced
  across the native/closure kind boundary), ok_class_freeze (the seal),
  ok_value_is_class. guard discipline per call for unrooted C state
- the embed test grows a Math class: construct, call, bind, isinstance,
  a mic-warmed loop, a native operator + entry, privacy, redeclaration
  and post-freeze refusals

gates: e2e 394x4 + unit x3 + embed x3
